      "shortest": true,
      "solution": "wcb = int(input())\n\nmatch wcb:\n    case 0 | 360:\n        print(\"N\")\n    case 90:\n        print(\"E\")\n    case 180:\n        print(\"S\")\n    case 270:\n        print(\"W\")\n    case _ if wcb < 90:\n        print(f\"N{wcb}E\")\n    case _ if wcb < 180:\n        print(f\"S{180 - wcb}E\")\n    case _ if wcb < 270:\n        print(f\"S{wcb - 180}W\")\n    case _ if wcb < 360:\n        print(f\"N{360 - wcb}W\")",
      "statement": "Create a program that converts a given Whole Circle Bearing (WCB) (an integer from 0 to 360) into its corresponding Reduced Bearing (RB) notation. The result should clearly state the quadrant direction (NθE, NθW, SθE, SθW) or the cardinal direction (N, E, S, W) if it falls exactly on a boundary (e.g. 90).",
