    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">Create a program that converts a given Whole Circle Bearing (WCB) (an integer from 0 to 360) into its corresponding Reduced Bearing (RB) notation. The result should clearly state the quadrant direction (N&theta;E, N&theta;W, S&theta;E, S&theta;W) or the cardinal direction (N, E, S, W) if it falls exactly on a boundary (e.g. 90).</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> An integer <var>wcb</var> for the whole circle bearing</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\"><strong>Line 1 :</strong> An string <var>rb</var> for the reduced bearing<br><br>For values between 0 and 90, 90 and 180, 180 and 270, and 270 and 360, use the format: [Cardinal_Start][Angle][Cardinal_End] (e.g., S45E).<br><br>For cardinal points (0, 90, 180, 270, 360), output the direction name only (e.g., E).</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\">0 &le; <var>wcb</var> &lt; 360<br>Input is always an integer.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">45</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-out\">N45E</pre>\n         </div>\n      </div>\n   </div>\n</div>"
